        "root_concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "section": "behavioral-economics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CLASSIC DEMONSTRATION — LINDA PROBLEM (Tversky & Kahneman 1983):\n  \"Linda is 31 years old, single, outspoken, and very bright. She majored in\n   philosophy. As a student, she was deeply concerned with issues of\n   discrimination and social justice, and also participated in antinuclear\n   demonstrations.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md#006",
      "path": [
        "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases, git-history:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases]",
        "canonical_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "current_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "id": "maxim:behavioral-economics:heuristics-biases",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "behavioral-economics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "section": "behavioral-economics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Rank in order of probability:\n  A. Linda is a bank teller.\n  B. Linda is a bank teller AND is active in the feminist movement."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md#007",
      "path": [
        "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases, git-history:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases]",
        "canonical_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "current_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "id": "maxim:behavioral-economics:heuristics-biases",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "behavioral-economics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "section": "behavioral-economics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "85-90% of subjects rank B > A — the CONJUNCTION FALLACY.\n  P(A ∩ B) ≤ P(A) always (by probability theory).\n  The conjunction cannot be more probable than either constituent.\n  But B \"represents\" the description better → judged more probable."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md#008",
      "path": [
        "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases, git-history:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases]",
        "canonical_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "current_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "id": "maxim:behavioral-economics:heuristics-biases",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "behavioral-economics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "section": "behavioral-economics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BASE RATE NEGLECT:\n  When given:\n  - Prior probability (base rate): P(H) = 0.01 (1% of population has disease X)\n  - Likelihood: P(positive test | H) = 0.95, P(positive test | not H) = 0.05"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md#009",
      "path": [
        "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases, git-history:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases]",
        "canonical_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "current_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "id": "maxim:behavioral-economics:heuristics-biases",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "behavioral-economics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "section": "behavioral-economics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Correct answer by Bayes: P(H | positive) = 0.95×0.01 / (0.95×0.01 + 0.05×0.99)\n                          = 0.00950 / (0.00950 + 0.04950) = 0.161"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md#010",
      "path": [
        "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases, git-history:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases]",
        "canonical_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "current_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "id": "maxim:behavioral-economics:heuristics-biases",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "behavioral-economics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "section": "behavioral-economics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Most people ignore the 1% base rate and respond ~95%.\n  The representativeness heuristic: \"the test is 95% accurate → positive result\n  means ~95% chance of disease.\" Base rate is discarded."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md#011",
      "path": [
        "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases, git-history:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases]",
        "canonical_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "current_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "id": "maxim:behavioral-economics:heuristics-biases",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "behavioral-economics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "section": "behavioral-economics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KAHNEMAN-TVERSKY FINDING: When case description is vivid and specific,\n  base rates are discounted. When no description is given, base rates are used."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md#012",
      "path": [
        "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases, git-history:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases]",
        "canonical_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "current_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "id": "maxim:behavioral-economics:heuristics-biases",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
