        "root_concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "section": "behavioral-economics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GAMBLER'S FALLACY:\n  \"The roulette has come up red 5 times in a row → black is due.\"\n  Representativeness: a sequence of random coin flips should \"look random\"\n  (alternating). A long run of heads doesn't represent randomness.\n  Therefore: perceive that tails is more likely after heads.\n  WRONG: each flip is independent; past outcomes don't affect future."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md#013",
      "path": [
        "03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases, git-history:behavioral-economics:03-heuristics-biases]",
        "canonical_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "current_path": "behavioral-economics/03-HEURISTICS-BIASES.md",
        "id": "maxim:behavioral-economics:heuristics-biases",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "behavioral-economics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[heuristics, biases]",
        "section": "behavioral-economics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Heuristics and Biases",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HOT HAND FALLACY (opposite direction):\n  \"He's made 6 shots in a row — he's on a hot hand. Pass to him.\"\n  Opposite error: past runs of success predict future success.\n  Gilovich, Vallone & Tversky (1985): no statistical hot hand in basketball.\n  BUT: Miller & Sanjurjo (2018) found a statistical artifact in GVT's test.\n  Current evidence: weak hot hand may exist in some sports contexts.\n```"
    }
